  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (best RNA-only: 0.5907 vs image-only: 0.2079), and multiprofile+avgpool is the best-known profile/aggregation combination (0.5907 vs 0.5191 for transformer, 0.4849 for singleprofile). The current best uses a simple linear PCA encoder. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) improve accuracy within the proven multiprofile+avgpool setup? This isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding profile and aggregation constant. Why this experiment: With 5 experiments remaining, the highest-expected-value move is to exploit the clearly superior multiprofile+avgpool RNA-only path and test whether a better encoder pushes accuracy above 0.59. If scvi_n200 helps, we can further refine; if not, we know the encoder is not the bottleneck and can pivot to testing scgpt or exploring whether multimodal fusion adds value on top of the best RNA configuration."
}

